        a="Searching for IT engineers, plural, usually means a bigger job or several sites: an office refit, a run of desks to set up, a portfolio of HMOs with router problems or a branch network that needs visiting in turn. We plan those as a schedule of visits with a named lead, so the same people return and the notes from one site carry over to the next.",
        x="For multi-site work, send a list of addresses with the issue at each. Grouping visits by area keeps travel down and lets engineers carry the right parts for the route.",
